// Data of the theorem graph (theorems.html): theorems, lemmas, corollaries and conjectures of statistics, MSC 2020 62.
// In English. Built on 3 November 2026.
//
// Model as in ../../algebraic-number-theory/data/theorem-graph.js (see its header comment): `premises` and `proof` are
// the standard textbook proof, named in `proofName`; further proofs in `alternativeProofs`; `foundation: true` marks a
// proof that rests on theory outside these graphs (named in `proof`). `area` is the three-character MSC class, as in
// data/concepts.js. `concepts` are ids of data/concepts.js or carry the prefix of another folder.
// `fromDefinitions: true` marks a theorem whose usual proof uses only definitions and axioms and no theorem.
//
// Conventions of this folder: the elementary properties of the expectation (linearity, monotonicity, expectation of a
// constant) count as part of the definition of the integral, as in the analysis folder, which lists no theorem for
// them. "Regular model" means the usual Cramér conditions: Θ open, the support of p_θ does not depend on θ, and
// differentiation in θ may be interchanged with integration over x. This interchange is an assumption of the
// theorems, not a step of their proofs.
//
// References: probability "pr:" (folder being built at the same time; ids expected there: laws of large numbers,
// central limit theorem, Slutsky, continuous mapping theorem, Jensen, law of total variance, martingale convergence,
// Donsker, …), linear algebra "la:" (spectral theorem, also being built), analysis "ana:" (Taylor, Cauchy–Schwarz,
// Radon–Nikodym, Fubini, projection theorem, Hahn–Banach), set theory "st:".
//
// Sources: Lehmann and Casella, Theory of Point Estimation (2nd ed. 1998); Lehmann and Romano, Testing Statistical
// Hypotheses (3rd ed. 2005); Casella and Berger, Statistical Inference (2nd ed. 2002); van der Vaart, Asymptotic
// Statistics (1998); Berger, Statistical Decision Theory and Bayesian Analysis (2nd ed. 1985); Ferguson, A Course in
// Large Sample Theory (1996); Anderson, An Introduction to Multivariate Statistical Analysis (3rd ed. 2003).
// Not checked by a specialist. Checked by ../../tests/check-theorems.js.

